// Where a list ends: the header update that finishes a growth, and the removal
// of the last cell.

list_wide(word p, word a, word z) {
  st64(p + 8, z);
  st64(p + 16, a);
} return void;

// The length is decremented first so that the cell read back is the one just
// dropped. docs/SPEC.md 5 traps on an empty list; here it walks off the front
// of the cells instead, for the same want of anywhere to report to that leaves
// indexing unchecked.
list_pop(int[] xs) {
  word p = l2w(xs);
  word ret_w = list_pop_at(p);
} return word ret_w;

// A conf.id list constant is locked once built on the hosted targets
// (docs/SPEC.md 8's "cannot mutate a constant list" trap) -- but there is
// nowhere to trap to here, the same reason list_get/list_set do not
// bounds-check (use/more/idx.id): no stderr, and nothing to exit to. So this
// is a no-op, kept only so the call idc_const_init makes on every target
// still links; mutating a freestanding list constant is unchecked, silently,
// the same as an out-of-range index here.
list_lock(int[] xs) {
} return void;
